# Op2_ApplyMoveBranchAtY: no corpus run calls it (ruling 5, 2; converted 2026-11-18, raw-reach-check). The case runs at Op2_BranchVar1Eq's first call ($002120): two
# operand words (limit, branch offset) and the object in a6; d1/d2 as they stand.
# The other cases set y ($42(a6), 16.16) beside the limit (the script word at a2) and the move d2,
# so each of the op's four paths runs: from below or above the limit, reaching it or not.
at $002120

case as_called

case below_reaches
w a6+$42 = {a2}+1
w a6+$44 = 0
reg d2 = $FFFE0000

case below_short
w a6+$42 = {a2}+2
w a6+$44 = 0
reg d2 = $FFFF0000

case above_reaches
w a6+$42 = {a2}-1
w a6+$44 = 0
reg d2 = $20000

case above_short
w a6+$42 = {a2}-2
w a6+$44 = 0
reg d2 = $10000
